# claude-trading-bot environment template.
#
# run.py's default (see DEFAULT_ENV_FILE) reads this from
# /home/ayman01323/ClaudeServer/runtime/claude-trading-bot.env on the Google
# server -- a path the operator/GPT provisions directly, outside git. This
# file is a template for what needs to be there, not something run.py loads
# by this filename. Set CLAUDE_BOT_ENV_FILE to point at a local copy instead
# for off-server testing.
#
# Never commit real values, never paste them into chat or source.
#
# run.py refuses to start (fail closed) if any REQUIRED variable below is missing.
# It never falls back to the production bot's own .env for these — see README.md
# "Isolation design" for why that matters.

# --- Isolation (OPTIONAL -- run.py fills these in deterministically if unset) ---
# Leave these blank/unset in the common case. run.py's
# _apply_deterministic_runtime_dir_defaults() defaults them to
# DEFAULT_RUNTIME_DIR/{CSVbot,data} -- the same directory this env file
# itself lives in, which is structurally guaranteed outside the git
# checkout. Manual entry here used to be the only thing keeping these paths
# safe; a Google-server preflight run found them simply blank, meaning
# every startup depended on that manual step being both present and
# correct. Only set these explicitly if you deliberately want a different
# location (e.g. local/off-server testing via CLAUDE_BOT_ENV_FILE) --
# whatever you set here always wins over the default.
#
# If you do set them explicitly: absolute paths, must NOT point inside the
# production CSVbot/ or data/ trees, and must NOT point inside the
# git-managed checkout (boot-trading-bot/...) at all -- the sync workflow
# refuses to sync if `git status --porcelain` shows any local changes, and
# that check does not exclude untracked files, so CSV/SQLite runtime state
# written inside the checkout would silently block every future sync.
CSV_DIR=
DATA_DIR=

# --- Telegram (REQUIRED) ---
# A dedicated bot token for this instance (create via @BotFather — do not reuse
# the production bot's token). Ask the operator which GitHub Secret / server
# secret location holds this; never paste the token itself into chat.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Chat id(s) that should receive Claude-bot reports. Comma-separated for multiple.
TELEGRAM_CHAT_IDS=

# --- Authorised chains (REQUIRED, real fail-closed execution boundary) ---
# Comma-separated, e.g. "solana". Enforced in solana_execution_risk_patch.py
# before every buy -- defaults to NOTHING authorised if unset or empty; this
# file does not choose a default value in code. The operator sets this.
# Currently only Solana has an execution guard wired at all (see
# solana_execution_risk_patch.py) -- listing an EVM chain here would not by
# itself let it trade, since no equivalent EVM guard exists yet.
AUTHORISED_CHAINS=

# --- Chain data providers (REQUIRED for whichever chains are authorised) ---
# Solana
SOLANA_RPC_URL=
SOLANA_WS_URL=
JUPITER_API_KEY=
# EVM RPC endpoints are CSV-driven, read from CSV_DIR/rpc_endpoints.csv by
# learnerbot/config.py::load_chains. KNOWN PATH MISMATCH (flagged in review,
# not yet resolved): the operator-provisioned CSV currently lives at
# /home/ayman01323/ClaudeServer/runtime/rpc_endpoints.csv (flat, sibling to
# this env file), while CSV_DIR above is .../runtime/CSVbot -- the loader
# will not find it there. Until the operator moves/symlinks it under CSV_DIR
# (or this code is changed to read an explicit alternate path), EVM chain
# config will not load even once AUTHORISED_CHAINS and an EVM guard exist.
# Not resolved here because the fix is the operator's call (move the file,
# symlink it, or designate a different path) rather than something to route
# around silently in code.

# --- Token/pool safety providers (REQUIRED) ---
GOPLUS_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# RugCheck.xyz is used unauthenticated by learnerbot/solana_pool_risk_gate.py;
# no key currently required there.

# --- Hard risk engine (REQUIRED — see risk_engine_guard.py) ---
# Consolidated per direct owner instruction (2026-08-26): there is exactly
# ONE number to set here. Position size, aggregate exposure, open-position
# count, and drawdown are all owner-approved fixed constants
# (OWNER_MAX_OPEN_POSITIONS=10, OWNER_MAX_POSITION_PCT=3.00%,
# OWNER_MAX_TOTAL_EXPOSURE_PCT=30.00%, OWNER_MAX_DRAWDOWN_PCT=20.00%) defined
# in risk_engine_guard.py, calculated dynamically against this one basis --
# not independently configurable, and not something this file, run.py, or
# any other code invents a default for. run.py refuses to start LIVE mode if
# this is absent/invalid, and solana_execution_risk_patch.py enforces the
# derived limits before every real buy, not just at startup.
#
# Slippage, price-impact, and minimum-liquidity are intentionally NOT part of
# this contract -- see risk_engine_guard.py's module docstring for exactly
# which reused, already-reviewed learnerbot code governs each of those
# instead (solana_pool_risk_gate.py's 200bps impact cap and LP-lock/liquidity
# checks, solana_live_executor.py's slippage parameter + post-execution
# validation). A second Claude-specific implementation of the same checks
# risked being redundant or, worse, inconsistent with logic already reviewed.
#
# This must be the actual owner-approved Claude trading capital/equity
# basis -- not a guess, not a value carried over from an old commit/runtime
# file.
CLAUDE_CAPITAL_BASIS_USD=

# --- Wallets ---
# Do NOT put a private key here. Wallets are created/imported through the bot's
# own encrypted wallet-store command flow once running (keyed to this instance's
# DATA_DIR, same mechanism production uses) — see README.md point 4.
#
# Identifies which row in this instance's isolated wallet-store CSV governs
# signing (see signing_interface.py). Any value matching Telegram-ID shape
# (digits, optionally one leading -) works — this bot is single-operator, not
# multi-tenant, so the exact number has no meaning beyond being a stable key.
# Until a signing key is actually provisioned for this id, SIGNER_READY stays
# false and broadcast stays unavailable, regardless of every other setting.
#
# Set this to the SAME value as the first entry in TELEGRAM_CHAT_IDS above --
# BUT verify it first, do not just assume it. learnerbot.cli's `run` command
# calls ensure_master_seed(app) on startup, which auto-creates this
# instance's sole ACTIVE/MASTER user from TELEGRAM_CHAT_IDS[0] IF users.csv
# is still empty at that point (learnerbot/user_registry.py:60). However:
# a real full-chain test run (verify_bootstrap_composition.py, see README)
# discovered that learnerbot/telegram_account_roles_patch.py -- a
# marker-gated ("`.telegram_roles_20260818_v1` in DATA_DIR") one-time
# migration meant for the production deployment -- replays against ANY
# fresh DATA_DIR lacking that marker file, including this instance's, and
# creates its OWN hardcoded user row (telegram_id 5882384847 as of this
# writing) independent of TELEGRAM_CHAT_IDS. Other marker-gated migrations
# in learnerbot's ~60-module patch chain may behave the same way and have
# not all been individually audited for this. Before setting this value for
# real, run `python verify_bootstrap_composition.py` (or `python run.py
# start` once, then check) against this instance's actual isolated
# CSV_DIR/DATA_DIR and read back learnerbot.user_registry.all_users() to see
# which telegram_id actually ends up as the sole enabled user -- then set
# CLAUDE_BOT_WALLET_OWNER_ID to match that, not to an assumed value.
# Mismatched values make SIGNER_READY fail closed on purpose (confirmed:
# this is exactly what happened in testing when the assumed value didn't
# match what the full chain actually produced).
CLAUDE_BOT_WALLET_OWNER_ID=

# --- Optional ---
ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=
